    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Family and possessives",
     "texto": [
      "To talk about our family we use the possessive adjectives **mi** (singular) and **mis** (plural):\n\n- **mi padre**, **mi madre**, **mi hermano**, **mi hermana**\n- **mis padres**, **mis hermanos**, **mis hijos**\n\nThe possessive agrees in number with the noun it modifies, but does not change according to gender: we say both *mi padre* and *mi madre*.\n\nTo give someone's name we use **se llama** (singular) or **se llaman** (plural): *Mi hermana se llama Mai*, *Mis padres se llaman Hoa y Nam*.\n\nIn Spanish, the masculine plural **los padres** includes the father and mother together, just as **los hermanos** can refer to brothers and sisters as a group."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Introducing family members",
     "texto": [
      "Notice the use of possessives and verb forms according to number:\n\n- **Singular**: Mi hermano se llama David.\n- **Plural**: Mis hermanos se llaman Carlos y Luis.\n\nUse *se llama* for one person and *se llaman* when introducing two or more people together."
     ],
